{
  "run_id": "PMC11355469__expert_context__web_decide_then_ground_b_o3mini__s1",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The overall high-temperature wear resistance of FeNiCrCoCu thin-film coatings is governed by the formation and stability of an adaptive protective oxide layer.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled pre-oxidation promotes formation of a continuous oxide layer before high-temperature wear testing.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9820961::web::025::3_1_phase_structure_and_morphology_of_co"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slight Cr enrichment would promote formation of a continuous, adherent protective oxide layer.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The adaptive oxide layer mainly contains oxides of Fe, Cr, and Cu.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The pre-formed oxide layer remains adherent during sliding wear.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adhesive, abrasive, fatigue, and oxidation wear can occur in heat-treated coatings of the type discussed in the cited study.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9820961::web::025::3_1_phase_structure_and_morphology_of_co",
        "PMC9820961::web::027::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide layer minimizes direct contact between the coating and counterface.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Minimizing direct contact through the oxide layer reduces adhesive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide layer reduces abrasive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elevated-temperature exposure can decrease coating hardness and intensify abrasive wear, cracking, and peeling.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9820961::web::023::3_1_phase_structure_and_morphology_of_co"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-temperature degradation involves grain coarsening and softening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9820961::web::023::3_1_phase_structure_and_morphology_of_co"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective oxide layer slows grain coarsening, softening, and other deleterious microstructural changes.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The pre-oxidized or Cr-enriched coating will have lower wear volume and wear rate than the as-deposited coating.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9820961::web::027::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified coating will retain a more continuous and adherent oxide scale after sliding.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified coating will exhibit a lower coefficient of friction at 600–800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed hypothesis is restricted to thin-film coatings on conventional metal substrates tested in sliding at 600–800 °C.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prior studies on similar systems indicate that a controlled oxide layer is beneficial at elevated temperature.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure to form a more stable oxide layer, or failure to obtain a statistically significant reduction in wear and friction relative to the as-deposited control, would falsify the hypothesis.",
      "field": "falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
